+# RC02 — dependency, secret and native lint checks
+
+**BLOCKED for full acceptance/release.** All checks local; public package/advisory downloads only. No live AI, credential validation or production operation.
+
+- Fresh npm audit:67 affected dependency nodes (50 high,17 moderate), rooted in five packages. Scoped `xcode → uuid11.1.1` override reduces the result to58 nodes (50 high,8 moderate); no forced Expo downgrade/major upgrade. Existing Xcode plugin tests run in Node, their real execution environment, and clean Expo prebuild passes. Jest initially selected uuid's ESM browser entry under React Native conditions; three build-plugin tests now explicitly use Node. No uuid mock or global resolver override.
+- `braces`, `node-forge`, `sprintf-js` have no patched release shown by the queried advisory/registry. `decode-uri-component0.5` changes to ESM default export, while installed query-string7 requires a callable CommonJS export. No untested override or forced Expo58 migration is retained. All unresolved nodes remain open, including build/test exposure.
+- Local Python audit: no known advisory among resolved distributions; application foodlogger is not on PyPI and was skipped by that scanner. Shipping Python3.12 image initially included vulnerable pip25.0.1; pinning26.2.1 removed its12 top-level advisory records. Whole-image scanning additionally exposed OS/embedded-installer dependencies; remediation and final counts are reported separately. A zero top-level pip-audit result is not a whole-image security verdict.
+- detect-secrets1.5.0 scanned4373 text blobs/current tracked files across all reachable local refs;213 binary blobs were omitted;0 candidates. `--no-verify` prevents network key validation. This is a bounded scanner result, not proof no secret ever existed or that external credentials were rotated.
+- Full Android lint reproduced Worklets/KaModule failure. A real diagnostic with `android.experimental.lint.version=8.13.2` also failed. No exclusions, disabled checks or dependency-source patches are retained. Earlier ineffective `-Dlint.version` and malformed version-number attempts are logged as failed diagnostics.
+
+[Every historical npm node and eight native warnings](dependency-disposition.md) remains mapped with original severity. The8 warnings retain RC06 ownership; RC06 is not started.
+
+## Sources and limits
+
+[uuid advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq), [braces advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm), [node-forge advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-86w9-cpqp-85rv), [sprintf advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c), [decode advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vcc3-ghjq-m6fr), [pip release notes](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/news/), [Trivy0.76.0](https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/releases/tag/v0.76.0), [upstream KaModule issue](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/430991549). The tracker search result mentions a fix but does not establish an Expo-compatible fixed toolchain. Actual local lint failure takes precedence.
+
+## Recovery
+
+Retain the patched uuid pair in package.json/package-lock.json and installer fix. Reverting these commits reinstates known findings. No database migration. Changing base OS/compiler/Expo for a larger remediation requires a new tested candidate and its native matrix; acceptance cannot be obtained by suppressing the scanner.
