+# RC05 — private-file cleanup across restarts
+
+Implemented locally; independent review/final verification pending at this draft. Physical force-kill/lock/reboot and OS backup privacy remain RC19.
+
+`storage/private-cleanup-recovery.ts` serializes recovery over the existing private-files matcher. A minimal global marker contains only `1`, no owner/token/content/path. Every cold start sweeps owned files even when the marker is absent/corrupt or could not be written. The matcher is unchanged: no general cache deletion and no draft/receipt deletion.
+
+AuthProvider performs recovery before account/navigation bootstrap. Failure is visible above signed-out navigation with Retry, without login or restoring credentials. Logout/deletion retain revocation even when cleanup fails. `storage/export.ts` waits for startup recovery, persists the marker before file creation, serializes share sheets, repeats owner/session checks and surfaces failed final deletion. Retry retains protection when account-export is compiled off; existing CSV cleanup remains available.
+
+## Tests
+
+New isolated module lifetimes plus a real multi-process Node/disk test cover abrupt termination after JSON/CSV creation, repeated deletion failure, corrupted/missing marker and a new signed-out recovery. Pending drafts/native receipts and unrelated files survive. Native File/AsyncStorage boundaries are adapters; mobile OS protection is not simulated as verified.
+
+Race tests cover logout during startup-marker persistence, old share sheet during account switch, session revocation, and cleanup with exports disabled. Existing HE/EN signed-out retry, logout/deletion, export/session tests run. Core RED4→GREEN;20 export/process/navigation checks pass; intermediate whole mobile454/90 passed. Final suite numbers are in the wave checkpoint.
+
+Three earlier regression fixtures needed adjustment because cold start now correctly erases files before logout; they now create a new session file before testing failed logout cleanup. Node-process tests use their proper Node test boundary. These are test harness corrections, not suppressed product failures.
+
+## Recovery
+
+Keep this recovery module, startup gate, signed-out Retry, narrow matcher and all P13 security fixes in any export-disabled rollback build. Do not use logout/account deletion as a substitute for erasure or claim external recipient copies were recalled. No schema migration. Historical P13 APK remains retained but is not automatically a safe RC03–05 operational downgrade; resolve pending edit/provenance compatibility first.
